This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   The user (こぎそ) asked, in Japanese: 「`brief.md`の要件を実装してください。」 with these conditional instructions:
   - **If `HARNESS.json` exists**: use `$atlas-design-system`, `$heroui-react`, `$ui-writing`; read `HARNESS_RESOLVED.json` and `DESIGN.md` before implementing; treat resolved pattern/variant/example/component/rule as authoritative; follow `heroui-react` for HeroUI API/compound components/standard styles, the design contract for Atlas-permitted choices, and `ui-writing` for Japanese UI copy; record referenced IDs and adopted decisions in the final report.
   - **If `HARNESS.json` does NOT exist**: implement using only `brief.md` as input.
   - **Either way**: preserve existing files' responsibilities, implement the required screen states and functionality, run the available verification commands (`pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test:run`, `pnpm build`) and resolve all errors. **Do not add dependencies.**

   **Verified: `HARNESS.json`, `HARNESS_RESOLVED.json`, and `DESIGN.md` do not exist** → the brief-only path applies.

   `brief.md` requirements (BtoB SaaS 請求書管理 screen for accounting staff):
   - List → find an invoice; select → separate detail screen showing content and payment status; edit the selected invoice; void mistakenly issued invoices.
   - List columns: 請求書番号、顧客名、発行日、金額、ステータス. Detail: 請求書番号、顧客名、発行日、支払期限、金額、ステータス、明細（品目、数量、単価）、メモ. Use the 4 fixture records in `src/fixtures.ts`.
   - Routes `/invoices` and `/invoices/:invoiceId`, handled with **HashRouter** so embedded demos can reload. Detail must offer a way back to the list.
   - List fetches summaries only; detail separately fetches the full record.
   - Edit screen changes 顧客名、支払期限、メモ. 支払期限 is required and entered as a date. No double submission while saving. On success reflect changes in the detail; on failure keep input and allow retry.
   - Void from detail, with a confirmation screen showing the target invoice number and outcome before committing (irreversible). Must use `voidInvoice` from `src/fixtures.ts`. On success notify completion and return to the list; on failure show the reason and allow retry.
   - Empty state when there are 0 invoices.
   - **Required states via URL `state` query**: `default`, `empty` on the list; `drawer-open`, `invalid-due-date`, `loading`, `success`, `failure`, `void-confirm` on the detail. `invalid-due-date` = due date empty or unreadable as a date; `void-confirm` = the void confirmation is open. **No dedicated state-switching UI on screen.**
   - Out of scope: creating invoices, recording/reconciling payments, report output/email/monthly reports, demo explanations, English subheadings, state-switch UI.
   - Tech: React, TypeScript, HeroUI; existing deps only; Build/TypeCheck/Test must pass; never show list and detail simultaneously; on both desktop and narrow screens they must be separate screens.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - React 19.2.8 + TypeScript 6.0.3 + Vite 8.2.2, Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`)
   - HeroUI v3.2.4 (`@heroui/react`, `@heroui/styles`) — compound components (`Table.Root/.ScrollContainer/.Content/.Header/.Column/.Body/.Row/.Cell`, `Card.Header/.Title/.Content`, `Alert.Indicator/.Content/.Title/.Description`, `Drawer.Backdrop/.Content/.Dialog/.Header/.Heading/.Body/.Footer`, `AlertDialog.Backdrop/.Container/.Dialog/.Header/.Icon/.Heading/.Body/.Footer`, `Chip.Label`, `Typography.Heading/.Paragraph`)
   - HeroUI v3 is built on react-aria-components 1.21.0; `Drawer.Root`/`AlertDialog.Root` are RAC `DialogTrigger` (accept `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`, first child = trigger, second = overlay)
   - RAC `RouterProvider` re-exported from `@heroui/react`, bridged to react-router `useNavigate`/`useHref` so HeroUI `Link href=...` does client-side navigation under HashRouter
   - `validationBehavior="aria"` on RAC `Form`/`TextField` to use custom validation instead of native constraint validation
   - HeroUI style variant vocabularies (verified by Node introspection): button variant = primary|secondary|tertiary|ghost|outline|danger|danger-soft; chip color = default|accent|success|warning|danger, variant = primary|secondary|tertiary|soft; alert status = default|accent|success|warning|danger; alertDialog size = xs|sm|md|lg|cover
   - Tailwind v4 theme tokens from `@heroui/styles`: `bg-background-secondary`, `bg-surface`, `text-muted`, `border-border`, `--color-*` (all verified present in the built CSS)
   - react-router-dom 7.18.3 `HashRouter`, `useLocation().search`, `useNavigate` with `{ replace, state }`
   - Vitest 4 + jsdom + @testing-library/react 16 + user-event 14
   - TDD per project rules; fixtures have module-level mutable state requiring `resetInvoiceRecords()` between tests

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`brief.md`** (read-only, the spec) — source of all requirements; no HARNESS files exist.

   - **`src/fixtures.ts`** (unmodified, must keep its responsibility)
     - Exports `InvoiceStatus = "下書き" | "送付済み" | "入金済み" | "期限超過"`, `InvoiceLineItem`, `InvoiceSummary` (id, invoiceNumber, customerName, issuedOn, amount, status), `InvoiceDetail`, `listInvoiceSummaries()`, `getInvoiceDetail(invoiceId)`, `VoidInvoiceResult = {ok:true} | {ok:false;reason:string}`, `voidInvoice(invoiceId, {simulateFailure?})`, `resetInvoiceRecords()`.
     - 4 records: `invoice_2026_0142` (INV-2026-0142 / 有限会社みなも / 2026-08-20 / due 2026-09-30 / ￥482,000 / 送付済み / 2 line items / note 「先方の締め日は月末。請求書番号を件名に入れる。」), `invoice_2026_0138` (INV-2026-0138 / 東雲テクノ株式会社 / 入金済み), `invoice_2026_0131` (INV-2026-0131 / 株式会社ひかり工房 / 期限超過), `invoice_2026_0150` (INV-2026-0150 / 若草エンジニアリング株式会社 / 下書き).
     - `voidInvoice` splices the record out of the module-level array.

   - **`src/format.ts`** (NEW) — display formatting + due-date validation, shared by list/detail/dialog.
     ```ts
     import type { InvoiceStatus } from "./fixtures";

     const ISO_DATE_PATTERN = /^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})$/;

     const currencyFormatter = new Intl.NumberFormat("ja-JP", {
       style: "currency",
       currency: "JPY",
     });

     /** 金額を「¥482,000」の形式にする。 */
     export function formatAmount(amount: number): string {
       return currencyFormatter.format(amount);
     }

     /** ISO形式の日付を「2026/08/20」の形式にする。読み取れない値はそのまま返す。 */
     export function formatDate(value: string): string {
       const matched = ISO_DATE_PATTERN.exec(value.trim());
       if (!matched) return value;

       const [, year, month, day] = matched;
       return `${year}/${month}/${day}`;
     }

     /**
      * 支払期限の入力値を検証する。
      * 未入力、または日付として読み取れない場合にエラー文言を返す。
      */
     export function validateDueDate(value: string): string | null {
       const trimmed = value.trim();
       if (!trimmed) return "支払期限を入力してください。";

       const matched = ISO_DATE_PATTERN.exec(trimmed);
       if (!matched) return "支払期限は2026-09-30のような形式で入力してください。";

       const [, year, month, day] = matched;
       const parsed = new Date(Date.UTC(Number(year), Number(month) - 1, Number(day)));
       const isRealDate =
         parsed.getUTCFullYear() === Number(year) &&
         parsed.getUTCMonth() === Number(month) - 1 &&
         parsed.getUTCDate() === Number(day);

       if (!isRealDate) return "支払期限に実在する日付を入力してください。";

       return null;
     }

     /** ステータスに対応するChipの色。 */
     export function statusChipColor(status: InvoiceStatus): "default" | "accent" | "success" | "danger" {
       switch (status) {
         case "入金済み": return "success";
         case "期限超過": return "danger";
         case "送付済み": return "accent";
         default: return "default";
       }
     }
     ```

   - **`src/screenState.ts`** (NEW) — parses the `state` query for the required screen states; reads both the HashRouter search and `window.location.search` for robustness.
     ```ts
     import { useLocation } from "react-router-dom";

     export const LIST_SCREEN_STATES = ["default", "empty"] as const;
     export const DETAIL_SCREEN_STATES = [
       "default", "drawer-open", "invalid-due-date", "loading",
       "success", "failure", "void-confirm", "void-failure",
     ] as const;

     export type ListScreenState = (typeof LIST_SCREEN_STATES)[number];
     export type DetailScreenState = (typeof DETAIL_SCREEN_STATES)[number];

     function readStateParam(routeSearch: string): string | null {
       const fromRoute = new URLSearchParams(routeSearch).get("state");
       if (fromRoute) return fromRoute;
       if (typeof window === "undefined") return null;
       return new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("state");
     }

     function resolveScreenState<T extends string>(routeSearch: string, allowed: readonly T[], fallback: T): T {
